Description: disable LTO so gkrust rustc stays under OOM-killer threshold
Author: Harkirat S Virk <harkiratsvirk@gmail.com>
Origin: local
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-05-15
Bug-Athena: Surfaced during GROUPS-01 phase 3 gnome build 2026-05-15
 NOT a packaging bug — this patch addresses a HOST-RESOURCE limit
 that surfaces as an opaque SIGKILL during the firefox-esr build:
 .
   error: could not compile `gkrust` (lib)
   Caused by:
     process didn't exit successfully: `... rustc ...` (signal: 9, SIGKILL: kill)
 .
 `gkrust` is Mozilla's monolithic Rust library for libxul.  Under
 `--enable-release` (default in `browser.mozconfig.in`) it compiles
 with LTO; the LTO link in a single rustc invocation peaks at
 ~6-8 GB resident.  With our `[Source]` parallelism running
 multiple rustc workers concurrently, total RAM saturates and the
 kernel OOM-killer fires.  cargo reports the SIGKILL as opaque
 `signal: 9` — the actual OOM message lands in host dmesg, not in
 the build log.
 .
 Fix: add `ac_add_options --disable-lto`.  Each gkrust rustc now
 peaks at ~2-3 GB instead of ~6-8 GB.  Trade-off: ~3-5% firefox
 runtime perf loss from no link-time optimisation across the Rust
 codebase.  Acceptable for an installable-via-tasksel browser
 where build reliability matters more than peak benchmark numbers.
 .
 Alternative considered and rejected: cap `CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=1` in
 `debian/rules` — single-threaded gkrust LTO compilation takes
 30-40 minutes vs ~7 min with `--disable-lto`, and a mozconfig
 knob is more discoverable than a buried env-var in rules.
 .
 Revert this patch only when paired with confirmation that the
 build host has ≥64 GB RAM headroom for parallel LTO rustc.
---
This patch header follows DEP-3: http://dep.debian.net/deps/dep3/
--- a/debian/browser.mozconfig.in
+++ b/debian/browser.mozconfig.in
@@ -2,6 +2,10 @@
 # packages for Debian or a derivative.
 ac_add_options --with-app-name=@browser@
 ac_add_options --enable-release
+# Athena: disable LTO on gkrust to keep per-rustc RAM ~2-3 GB rather
+# than ~6-8 GB.  Without this, the gkrust LTO link is OOM-killed on
+# 16-32 GB build hosts with our [Source] parallelism settings.
+ac_add_options --disable-lto
 ac_add_options --enable-default-toolkit=cairo-gtk3-wayland
 ac_add_options --with-google-location-service-api-keyfile=$topsrcdir/debian/google.key
 ac_add_options --with-google-safebrowsing-api-keyfile=$topsrcdir/debian/google.key
